cff-version: 1.2.0
message: 'To cite the graphlearnR package in publications use:'
type: software
license: GPL-3.0-only
title: 'graphlearnR: Graph Machine Learning and Geometric Deep Learning in R'
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-11-12'
abstract: >-
  A native R framework for machine learning on graphs, built on the torch
  package without a Python dependency. Provides validated graph data
  structures with explicit 1-based indexing, conversion from igraph, edge
  lists and sparse matrices, mini-batching, scatter aggregation and message
  passing, graph neural network layers (GraphSAGE, GCN, GIN, GAT, GATv2,
  transformer convolution, NNConv, RGCN), pooling, neighbor sampling,
  leakage safe splits, heterogeneous and temporal graphs, graph
  transformers with structural encodings, a training loop for node, edge,
  link and graph tasks, evaluation metrics, and explanations.
authors:
